import{_ as a,o as t,c as n,ak as o}from"./chunks/framework.B8jO0odJ.js";const u=JSON.parse('{"title":"Web3 visual-design handoff","description":"Generated 22 October 2026 using built-in image generation. These are original concept images for the new GDD, not existing Android-build screenshots and not imported Unity ass","frontmatter":{"title":"Web3 visual-design handoff","description":"Generated 22 October 2026 using built-in image generation. These are original concept images for the new GDD, not existing Android-build screenshots and not imported Unity ass","source":"docs/media/gdd/gameplay-first/notes/visual-web3-notes.md","category":"Other documents","sourceUpdated":"2026-10-22T22:46:54+08:00","outline":[2,3]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"content/docs/media/gdd/gameplay-first/notes/visual-web3-notes.md","filePath":"content/docs/media/gdd/gameplay-first/notes/visual-web3-notes.md"}'),i={name:"content/docs/media/gdd/gameplay-first/notes/visual-web3-notes.md"};function r(s,e,l,c,d,h){return t(),n("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[o('<div><h1 id="web3-visual-design-handoff">Web3 visual-design handoff<a class="header-anchor" href="#web3-visual-design-handoff" aria-label="Link to this section">​</a></h1><p>Generated 22 October 2026 using built-in image generation. These are original concept images for the new GDD, not existing Android-build screenshots and not imported Unity assets.</p><h2 id="deliverables">Deliverables<a class="header-anchor" href="#deliverables" aria-label="Link to this section">​</a></h2><ul><li>docs/media/gdd/gameplay-first/web3-world.png — compact restoration harbor, workshop, merchant and Sean/Explorer. 1672 × 941 PNG. Caption: &quot;Web3 restoration harbor concept. A short route links arrival, the lantern merchant and the unlit workshop.&quot;</li><li>docs/media/gdd/gameplay-first/web3-purchase.png — three purchase UI states, 1672 × 941 PNG. Caption: &quot;Purchase-state design study. Review 8 coins plus 1 gas, wait for validation, then receive Lantern #014 and a 3-coin remaining balance.&quot;</li></ul><h2 id="design-rationale-and-accuracy">Design rationale and accuracy<a class="header-anchor" href="#design-rationale-and-accuracy" aria-label="Link to this section">​</a></h2><ul><li>Existing approved reference images were inspected: current-visuals/isometric-exploration.png and dialogue-overlay.png. Their blue-haired yellow-clad Explorer, white cyan-screen robot, faceted stone, and navy/cyan overlay identity informed this work.</li><li>World image is a compact isometric landmass, not a large production level commitment. The merchant lantern is the sole lit quest lantern; workshop hook is empty and interior dim. The environment may be simplified further for mobile.</li><li>Intended full-vision scene sequence: arrival/tutorial → resident reward → merchant review/sign → pending → confirmed ownership → equip/install lantern → workshop restoration.</li><li>UI sheet is three sequential mockups arranged side by side for comparison, not a proposed simultaneous three-column phone screen.</li><li>Review screen uses 12 Chain Coins, price 8, gas 1, total 9, final balance 3. Pending does not claim ownership. Confirmed asset card identifies Lantern #014 and owner.</li><li>NFT is the unique ownership record, not the receipt or physical lantern itself. The shipped concept explanation must make this distinction explicit.</li><li>Currency, signature, ledger and NFT are entirely simulated. No real wallet, keys, seed phrase or cryptocurrency required.</li><li>Equipping and walking do not incur gas. The 1-coin network fee is an intentionally simplified tutorial value, not a real-network claim.</li><li>Production needs separate Cancel/back navigation, insufficient-balance feedback, interrupted-purchase resume, idempotent confirmation, accessible text scaling and tested touch targets. These were not all shown in this focused sheet.</li><li>The review-and-sign button signifies a signature step; the GDD must distinguish private signing key, public verification and receiving address in the full curriculum.</li><li>Main scene camera was corrected after generation to remove horizon and cinematic perspective. First discarded draft also had lit workshop lanterns, removed in the final.</li><li>UI background character has somewhat older/taller proportions than the scene Explorer. Treat this as a style-review caveat, not an approved new character model.</li><li>No implementation or measured performance is represented. Production art must be made as separate modular meshes/materials and actual UI, not derived by pretending these flattened PNGs are ready 3D assets.</li><li>Source: AI-generated original concepts, using the team&#39;s inspected references for direction. Production owner/licensing clearance and final import settings remain a team handoff decision. Proposed documentation import: preserve aspect ratio, do not crop critical UI labels; no Unity texture budget claim.</li></ul><h2 id="exact-generation-prompt--world-initial">Exact generation prompt — world initial<a class="header-anchor" href="#exact-generation-prompt--world-initial" aria-label="Link to this section">​</a></h2><p>Use case: stylized-concept Asset type: landscape game environment concept for Chainy educational Android game&#39;s GDD, not a screenshot and not production game assets. Primary request: a compact Web3 restoration harbor and workshop teaching route, fixed orthographic isometric camera at about 40 degrees downward, wide overview suitable to explain a small playable level. One small explorer with blue faceted hair, a yellow coat, yellow backpack, dark boots; a friendly small white faceted robot guide Sean with a black screen face and cyan eyes, cyan joints. They stand on a readable pale stone path connecting the harbor arrival, merchant stall, and dark workshop. Scene: Angular weathered stone island terraces, restrained olive grass, teal-blue water, short wooden pier, a single compact merchant stall with ONE distinct lantern on display, a dim workshop with an empty lantern bracket just outside its entrance, ruin pillars, sparse angular trees, clear short footpaths without a maze. An island awaiting restoration, welcoming not ruined by war. Style: polished faceted low-poly game concept; planar stone and foliage, restrained painterly surface detail, long soft-edged late-afternoon shadows, controlled cyan glow only on a small interaction marker, atmospheric blue distance. Tiny characters relative to environment, readable traversable space. Composition: wide landscape 16:9, entire compact route visible in one clear connected landmass; no panels or inset art. No labels, no text, no HUD, no interface, no logos, no watermark. Do not depict cryptocurrency symbols or financial charts. NOT voxel, NOT blocky Minecraft, NOT glossy toy diorama, NOT rounded Pixar, NOT close third-person view. Use reference character/color identity described, but create a new original harbor layout. Preserve empty workshop bracket as the quest destination.</p><h2 id="exact-correction-prompt--world-selected-final">Exact correction prompt — world selected final<a class="header-anchor" href="#exact-correction-prompt--world-selected-final" aria-label="Link to this section">​</a></h2><p>Edit this Chainy Web3 harbor concept. Preserve the blue-haired yellow-clad small explorer, white cyan-eyed robot Sean, merchant stall, stone paths, workshop, faceted low-poly materials, color palette and original subjects. Change camera to a TRUE ORTHOGRAPHIC ISOMETRIC OVERVIEW about 40 degrees DOWNWARD: no visible sun, no horizon, no sky, no panoramic sea cliffs or cinematic perspective; top of frame is surrounding blue water, land shown as compact island from above. Preserve readable short connected paths between pier, merchant and workshop. At the workshop REMOVE both the lantern hanging outside and lit lantern inside: show an EMPTY black metal lantern hook on wall, and the workshop interior visibly dim/unrestored. Keep one visible lit lantern on the merchant stall only. No additional lanterns elsewhere. Limit tiny clutter and excessive stone detail to clean restrained low-poly planes. This is a landscape GDD concept, not game screenshot. No UI, no text, no watermark.</p><h2 id="exact-generation-prompt--purchase-sheet">Exact generation prompt — purchase sheet<a class="header-anchor" href="#exact-generation-prompt--purchase-sheet" aria-label="Link to this section">​</a></h2><p>Use case: ui-mockup Asset type: landscape high-fidelity game UI DESIGN SHEET for Chainy&#39;s GDD; three sequential state studies, NOT one live screen. Primary request: show Web3 lantern purchase with exactly three large panel studies from left to right: REVIEW &amp; SIGN, PENDING, CONFIRMED. A faded faceted isometric harbor scene (stone ruin paths, olive grass, cyan water, wooden merchant stall) anchors the sheet. Small blue-haired yellow-clad Explorer and friendly white cyan-screen robot in background. UI foreground takes priority. Minimal dark navy panels with thin cyan angular edges, pale readable mobile typography, generous spacing, gold coin icon, lantern equipment icon. Composition: 16:9 landscape. Top header small: &quot;WEB3 — PURCHASE FLOW&quot;; beneath, large three panels and simple rightward arrows between them; panel 1 is slightly wider for costs. Clearly separated state studies. Flat clean layout with no phone frames, large touch buttons, no tiny annotations. Exact text: Header: &quot;WEB3 — PURCHASE FLOW&quot; Small subtitle: &quot;Concept • Simulated currency only&quot; LEFT panel heading &quot;1 REVIEW &amp; SIGN&quot; &quot;Wallet: 12 Chain Coins&quot; &quot;Lantern #014&quot; &quot;Price 8&quot; &quot;Gas 1&quot; &quot;Total 9&quot; &quot;After purchase: 3&quot; Large button &quot;Review &amp; sign&quot; MIDDLE panel heading &quot;2 PENDING&quot; A simple outlined progress circle. &quot;Awaiting validation&quot; &quot;Ownership not confirmed&quot; RIGHT panel heading &quot;3 CONFIRMED&quot; &quot;Wallet: 3 Chain Coins&quot; Lantern illustration with small asset card reading &quot;Lantern #014&quot; and &quot;Owner: You&quot; Button &quot;View ledger&quot; Button &quot;Equip&quot; Constraints: all numerical values and labels verbatim, no other quantities, no reward claim, no seed phrase/private key display, no crypto logos, no charts. Distinguish the uniquely numbered lantern ownership asset from a payment receipt. Never show gas cost for walking, reading or equipping. Do not show the item equipped in PENDING. Feedback uses text and icons not color alone. Consistent restrained low-poly art with existing blue-haired yellow explorer/white cyan-faced robot. No cartoon toy diorama, no rounded glossy plastic, no watermark.</p></div>',1)])])}const m=a(i,[["render",r]]);export{u as __pageData,m as default};
